{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5z1N8MYVhsRTeEesdg54t","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"65e856c0f7419e9995ceeafda502adf102791d26","date":"2026-05-13T22:49:15+03:00","message":"(chore) Raise vitest testTimeout to 30s (#554)","refs":"","body":"The default 5s per-test timeout fires on CI for the StockItemsTable\n'renders initial state and UI elements correctly' test, which is a\nuserEvent-heavy test that completes in well under a second locally\nbut takes ~6s on GitHub Actions runners.\n\nThe local-vs-CI gap is vitest's per-test overhead (ESM resolution and\nSWC transforms) combined with slower CI hardware. The same pattern\nshowed up across openmrs-esm-patient-chart and was addressed there\nwith the same global bump.\n\nRaise testTimeout to 30s. Real hangs will still fail loudly; this\nonly forgives slow-but-progressing tests.\n\nSee https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/actions/runs/25805834552/job/75808178552\nfor the failing run.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"79953cf66885a70e1b0430f14d82d9fb8b4de86e","date":"2026-05-13T16:45:28+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#552)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning stock-management\nwith the patterns adopted by openmrs-esm-core, openmrs-esm-billing-app,\nand the other in-flight migrations.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom, and\n  @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env;\n  bump @testing-library/dom (10.4.0 to 10.4.1) and\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (5.x to 6.x) so the /vitest subpath is\n  available.\n- Add vitest.config.ts with the standard O3 vitest setup: jsdom\n  environment, .scss/.css aliased to identity-obj-proxy with an\n  anchored ^.*.s?css$ regex, @openmrs/esm-framework aliased to its\n  mock, react-i18next aliased to the local __mocks__ file, @mocks\n  and @tools aliases for the path shortcuts already in use, and\n  fakeTimers.toFake limited to the timers we actually fake (excludes\n  queueMicrotask which otherwise breaks React's scheduler).\n- Add tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  (which is enough for tsc to pick up the matcher type extension),\n  register afterEach(cleanup), and rewrite the ResizeObserver mock\n  as a class (Carbon's TextArea calls it with `new`).\n- Convert the eighteen test files to the vitest API: explicit imports\n  for describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach where used), jest.*\n  swapped for vi.*, jest.Mock type alias replaced with Mock from\n  vitest. Inline component factories of the form vi.mock(name, () =>\n  () => <jsx />) wrapped in { default: ... } since vitest requires\n  the factory to return a module object. The vi.mock('./hooks/\n  useParties', () => vi.fn()) factory similarly wrapped to expose a\n  default export.\n- Update the danger-button selector in stock-sources-delete.test.tsx\n  to /danger\\s*delete/i: the newer testing-library no longer joins\n  the visually-hidden \"danger\" prefix and the visible \"Delete\" with\n  a space when computing the accessible name.\n- Delete jest.config.js.\n\nAll 112 tests pass; lint and typescript checks are green.\n\n* (chore) Tidy up vitest config and test imports\n\nFollow-ups to the jest→vitest migration:\n\n- vitest.config.ts: drop `globals: true` (every test file imports\n  describe/it/expect/vi/test explicitly, so the global is dead),\n  drop the unused `@tools` alias (no `from '@tools'` in src), and\n  add `resolve.mainFields: ['module', 'main']` so vitest picks\n  @carbon/react's ESM entry. The CJS entry's `var l10n =\n  require('flatpickr/dist/l10n/index')` only exposes `default`,\n  leaving `l10n['en']` undefined and producing 300+ \"flatpickr:\n  invalid locale undefined\" stderr lines per `--reporter=verbose`\n  run.\n- 10 test files: strip the unused `test` named import from the\n  `vitest` import line. ESLint won't catch these because\n  `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` is disabled in .eslintrc.\n- 3 test files (step1, user-selector, stock-sources-items-table):\n  drop redundant `__esModule: true` from `vi.mock` factory\n  returns — vitest doesn't need the marker when the factory\n  returns `{ default: ... }`.\n\n* (fix) Silence React warnings from stock-item-details\n\nTwo pre-existing warnings surfaced once vitest started routing\nper-test stderr through its verbose reporter:\n\n1. `forwardRef render functions accept exactly two parameters` —\n   StockItemDetails was wrapped in forwardRef but its render\n   function only took `(props)` and no caller passed a ref. Drop\n   the dead wrap and inline-type the props.\n\n2. `React does not recognize the 'controllerName' prop on a DOM\n   element` — ControlledTextInput spread `{...props}` onto the\n   inner Carbon `<TextInput>`, leaking the `controllerName` and\n   `control` react-hook-form props through to the DOM `<input>`.\n   Destructure them out before spreading. The sibling\n   ControlledRadioButtonGroup already does this; the wrappers\n   now agree.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for vitest config aliases\n\nvitest.config.ts used new URL(...).pathname for the react-i18next\nand @mocks alias replacements. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/...\nwhich is not a valid filesystem path, so Vite's resolver fails.\nAdd a small fileURLToPath helper and route every URL-based path\nthrough it, matching the pattern adopted in openmrs-esm-form-builder.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c67e47060f34697bd5e9aa63389a35fc5df2eed8","date":"2026-05-05T09:15:40+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality (#541)","refs":"","body":"* O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality\n\n* Response to Comments","authorName":"Lubwama Samuel","authorEmail":"lubwamasamuel3@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f6fc80647842ad34e8364caae0e84d9c880f7505","date":"2026-02-08T10:45:09+03:00","message":"fix stock location underfetching (#452)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"57762d8996ba512029e9c34976d2ae3ae2a8af61","date":"2025-06-23T09:38:12+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-4823: Change metrics labels to ‘Understocked’ and ‘Overstocked’ (#312)","refs":"","body":"* (refactor) refactor: update stock management metric labels for clarity\n\n* (refactor) updated the translation\n\n* (refactor) Ranming the terminology of the span\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Fredrick Kioko","authorEmail":"67967749+its-kios09@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"cfb2c783cf54bb705d9022b3c5eb03cd51b58d14","date":"2025-05-22T11:02:08-04:00","message":"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#297)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"9c2af2f07c634e9214b726ba246584d2f30acf28","date":"2025-05-20T17:26:09+03:00","message":"(fix) Remove non-functional view links from stock metrics cards (#296)","refs":"tag: v3.1.0","body":"Removes the `View ->` links from the metrics cards on the stock management dashboard. These links don't currently navigate anywhere. Removing them clears up potential confusion for users.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e46300618d84977661fca9f699ef1c3d408f188c","date":"2025-05-20T09:17:19-04:00","message":"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#295)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"c96b7ca1adc10e9f6b790d83506400f146db498b","date":"2025-05-20T10:58:42+03:00","message":"(chore) Release v3.1.0 (#294)","refs":"","body":"Cuts a minor release of Stock Management with the following draft changelog:\n\n* (feat) Add Balance column on stock and bin cards by @Ogollah in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/263\n* (feat) O3-4685: Use workspaces instead of overlays by @jabahum in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/268\n* (feat) Stock operations table UI enhancements by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/280\n* (feat) O3-4695: Improve create stock report and add stock sources form layouts by @Munyua123 in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/281\n* (feat) Additional visual tweaks by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/285\n* (feat) Add page header to stock management dashboard by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/289\n\n* (refactor) O3-4695: Improve stock user role scope workspace form layout by @Munyua123 in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/277\n* (refactor) Various tweaks to overview page by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/278\n* (refactor) Remove custom overlay implementation by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/290\n* (refactor) Improve component organization and naming consistency by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/291\n* (refactor) O3-4693: Refactor stock items form to use workspace system instead of overlays by @Omoshlawi in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/275\n\n* Restore: (fix) Various test and styling fixes (#282) by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/283\n* (fix) Various test and styling fixes by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/282\n* (fix) O3-4699-Restored step-by-step form validation to ensure each step is validated before allowing progression to the next. by @Omoshlawi in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/279\n* (fix) Remove stock metrics loading spinner to prevent layout shift by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/286\n* (fix) Fix translations and UI consistency by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/293\n* (fix) Clean up UI inconsistences by @jabahum in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/292\n* Revert 03-4626 - Prevent Duplicate Batch Numbers in Opening and Receipt Stock Operations by @Omoshlawi in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/287\n\n* (chore) Enforce consistent type imports by @denniskigen in https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management/pull/272","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b20f85d0eb11170c0577c24f13bd9b1e7e70e264","date":"2025-05-16T14:57:33+03:00","message":"(feat) Additional visual tweaks (#285)","refs":"","body":"This PR makes a few visual adjustments to the User role scopes table UI. These include:\n\n- Replacing the Carbon `Button` component used in the delete and edit actions menu with the `IconButton` component. This allows us to take advantage of the IconButton's spacing, alignment, and tooltip features.\n- Adding consistent sizing and spacing for arrow icons in the Locations column.\n- Updating translation keys for better consistency.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1434d8eebea114f5d44893768c0e26e748cf6514","date":"2025-05-16T14:48:11+03:00","message":"(fix) Remove stock metrics loading spinner to prevent layout shift (#286)","refs":"","body":"Removes the loading spinner from stock metrics component to eliminate layout shift when data loads. This improves the user experience by maintaining a stable layout during data fetching.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"250fbf08e388f60c17923e11d84d294ba2950afd","date":"2025-04-15T18:21:34+03:00","message":"(refactor):03-4505-Refactor stock operations forms for ease of maintenance (#258)","refs":"","body":"* added horizontal tabs for stock operations\n\n* Lauching workspace form on select stock item bt form unimplemented\n\n* reafctored stock operation form ui bt has bugs\n\n* fiexed stock operation update bug\n\n* fixed eslint dependancy array\n\n* Contitionaly rendering date firled based on schema as well\n\n* feat: add canEdit prop to StockItemForm and StockItemsAddition components for conditional rendering\n\n* feat: implement stock operation form utilities and enhance component structure;\n\n* feat: add hooks for user search and operation type permissions; enhance base operation detail form by making  conditional rendering of fields and ensuring autofeeling\n\n* feat: add empty state component and styles; linked stock item workspace to empty state add buton and launching well\n\n* feat: refactor stock operation components; add QuantityUomCell and StockOperationItemCell, enhance StockAvailability with error handling and loading states\n\n* feat: add BatchNoSelector component and hook for managing stock item batch numbers;\n\n* feat: enhance stock operation forms with improved styling and new submission step component\n\n* feat: add approval requirement radio buttons and conditional action buttons in stock operation submission form\n\n* feat: refactor stock operation dialog handling and improve type management in stock operations;seperate concerns on hook\n\n* feat: add delete functionality for stock operation items and enhance utility functions for object manipulation\n\n* feat: add quantity UoM selector component and integrate it into stock item form; clean up batch no selector\n\n* feat: clean up imports and improve component structure in stock operation forms\n\n* feat: enhance stock operation forms with new related link component and improve styling; refactor stock operation issue button\n\n* feat: enhance loading indicators in selectors and add unit tests for user and batch number selectors\n\n* feat: improve user selector component with loading and error states; enhance unit tests for better coverage\n\n* test: refactor and enhance unit tests for stock operation reason and user selectors; improve mock implementations\n\n* feat: add readOnly property to input components and enhance stock operation form utility functions\n\n* feat: add stock operation status components and styles; enhance stock operation form with additional tab functionality\n\n* refactor: improve stock operation form functionality and cleanup unused code\n\n* refactor: update stock operation forms and styles, remove unused components\n\n* refactor: reorganize imports and enhance loading state accessibility in stock operation forms;Fix undefined bug in operation form submision\n\n* update labelText to titleText in StockOperationReasonSelector component\n\n* refactor: remove unused stock operation components and styles\n\n* refactor: remove disabled state from stock operation form used for testing\n\n* refactor: remove unused qty-uom and batch-no selectors along with their styles and tests\n\n* refactor: remove unused component StockOperationReasonSelector replacing it with refactored version\n\n* refactor: remove unused stock item selector components and tests; added step 1 and 2 tests\n\n* refactor: update step 2 tests to use new stock item hooks and remove deprecated code; add step 3 test file\n\n* refactor: remove unused EmptyState component and its styles; add mock for operation types\n\n* refactor: remove unused addOrEditStockOperation function and related imports\n\n* fix broken batch-no-selector tests\n\n* fix: correct spelling of initialValue in BatchNoSelector and related components\nfeat: add StockOperationItemBatchNoCell and StockoperationItemExpiryCell components\nrefactor: integrate new components into StockOperationItemsFormStep\n\n* stock issue operation usecase handled to capture related requisition,\n\n* refactor: update stock operation components to use unified data fetching and improve error handling","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c613cb7b24e174499e6c8d8f3187ff7f532bd3d3","date":"2024-12-02T10:19:22+03:00","message":"(feat)- O3-3966: At stock requisition, user should be able to see the number of the stock item and its availability (#237)","refs":"","body":"* View number of the stock item and its availability\r\n\r\n* Total Quantity from all batches of stock item\r\n\r\n* styling","authorName":"Trevor Antony","authorEmail":"61781670+TrevorAntony@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"84b88be2d745f9eabe2ef72cc6fe76c11acf8c2b","date":"2024-10-01T09:24:35+03:00","message":"(Test): O3-3756: Add unit tests for the add a new Stock item (#217)","refs":"","body":"* Add unit tests for the add a new Stock item\r\n\r\n* firevent to userevent refactor\r\n\r\n* build error fix\r\n\r\n* Avoid direct node access","authorName":"Trevor Antony","authorEmail":"61781670+TrevorAntony@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"27b86c6a2192a631a35b0b1d14bde30afa476b9b","date":"2024-10-01T09:05:53+03:00","message":"(Tests) 03-3758: stock operation tabs StockOperationSubmission test (#214)","refs":"","body":"* tests for the stock operation tabs StockOperationSubmission\r\n\r\n* change occurrences of the fireEvent and adopt userEvent to simulate user interaction.\r\n\r\n* lint and fix build fail\r\n\r\n* lint and fix build fail","authorName":"Lucy Jemutai","authorEmail":"130601439+lucyjemutai@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"32b052901bfb955247a61f38f766caee4d4c81ec","date":"2024-09-27T10:50:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Disable number input scroll wheel functionality (#226)","refs":"","body":"This PR disables the scroll wheel functionality in [NumberInput](https://react.carbondesignsystem.com/?path=/docs/components-numberinput--overview) fields in the Stock Management app by setting the `disableWheel` prop. Before this change, when a NumberInput field was focused and the user scrolled past with their mouse wheel, the value in the input would increment or decrement. This can lead to accidental value changes that the user might overlook. Setting the prop fixes makes the NumberInput ignore mouse wheel events when focused, reducing the likelihood of unintentional value changes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"2cca64059c83813fb8a9355a65fd23ea902d4953","date":"2024-08-19T10:26:28+03:00","message":"Fixed Form State on Assign Responsible Person as Default Person on Stock Management Operations based on User Login (#200)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Captain David","authorEmail":"75360744+DavidSaruni@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"71a799f5af31bd3c292680985acc58f02769477a","date":"2024-08-12T10:00:41+03:00","message":"Remove userscope which is causing the page to load endlessly (#191)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"kyampeire Hadijah","authorEmail":"30952856+hadijahkyampeire@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"bbe8e0473f9f55ad9e81ca53bfc52da2e4f51d2a","date":"2024-08-07T14:15:19+03:00","message":"(feat) Assign Responsible Person as Default Person on Stock management operations base on User Login (#186)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Fredrick Kioko","authorEmail":"67967749+its-kios09@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"735237a25ab0f3f5496198d07264e74b5ee26ba8","date":"2024-08-07T14:08:17+03:00","message":"O3-3695-Show received stock items list after a stock issue operations has been disp (#179)","refs":"","body":"* O3-3695\r\n\r\nShow received stock items list after a stock issue operations has been dispatched.\r\nIt allows A user  to see alist of stock items he/she received  only after a completed ,dispatched stock issue\r\n\r\n* Changes made to make it visible for only stock issue operation.\r\n\r\n* received items show depending on the permission being true or false.\r\n\r\n* fix bug\r\n\r\n* The \"Received Items\" tab now is only visible on Complete or Dispatched stock issues.\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: jabahum <jabajnan8@gmail.com>","authorName":"TrevorAntony","authorEmail":"61781670+TrevorAntony@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c1a25b4b1618f54a7c3bb511d90d8d064cb5cca4","date":"2024-07-31T20:10:24+03:00","message":"O3-3675-Allow user to only perform stock operation in assigned location (#172)","refs":"origin/O3-3688-Some-tabs-are-covered-while-editing-a-stock-item","body":"","authorName":"Makombe Kennedy","authorEmail":"kennedymakombe@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5130a768621eecb50378e95d4faa77e11c753897","date":"2024-07-28T00:44:46+03:00","message":"(fix)O3-3662:Prefill the user scope roles when editing (#163)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Makombe Kennedy","authorEmail":"kennedymakombe@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5160d131bbd2974c197f8708d3f2bb7f1c28ca36","date":"2024-07-27T21:18:56+03:00","message":"(fix)O3-366:Disable action buttons for a logged in user in user role scope (#164)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Makombe Kennedy","authorEmail":"kennedymakombe@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ce2227eff8ebc6f36e56f9cf1378f74696153b50","date":"2024-07-02T17:53:30+03:00","message":"fix:Made UI issues on stock module (#150)","refs":"","body":"* Made the datepicker in stock operations responsive\r\n\r\n* Replace nondrugs with Pharmaceuticals and removed the repetitive stock in stock module menu\r\n\r\n* Limited the expiring items in stock home overview to only first 5 items\r\n\r\n* correction for \"Limited the expiring items in stock home overview to only first 5 items\" commit\r\n\r\n* fix/remove-repeating-stock-label (#148)\r\n\r\n* fixed ci/cd error for slice(0,5)\r\n\r\n* fix pagination (#151)\r\n\r\n* fixed build issues\r\n\r\n* fixed conflict in #150\r\n\r\n* Made the datepicker in