{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0126UZCKsGSGmcWETDAXviUV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"12a145551cda444d3c1a79e62699b7735b8dc892","date":"2026-09-30T19:38:55+03:00","message":"(feat) Migrate stock management to workspace v2 (#661)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Migrate stock management to workspace v2\n\nMoves the stock management workspaces from the v1 workspace API to\nworkspace v2. openmrs-esm-core#1893 removes the v1 API from the framework.\n\nroutes.json now declares a stock-management-group overlay group with one\nwindow per workspace. The windows keep the extra-wide width and the\nmaximize button the v1 workspaces had. The group uses the default\napp-wide persistence. A closable group hides the header close button on\ndesktop and expects the action menu to provide it, and this app has no\naction menu.\n\nEach workspace component now takes Workspace2DefinitionProps, reads its\nprops from workspaceProps, and renders inside Workspace2. The titles\nthat callers used to pass as workspaceTitle are now set by the\nworkspaces themselves, using the same translation keys. Launch sites\ncall launchWorkspace2, and the two launch helpers no longer take a t\nargument.\n\nThe stock rule form is now a child workspace of the stock item\nworkspace, opened with launchChildWorkspace from useWorkspace2Context.\nIt used to replace the stock item form. Now closing it returns to the\nstock item. After a new stock item is saved, the form relaunches the\nstock item workspace with the saved item instead of closing and\nreopening it, because the two v2 calls are async and could race.\n\nRemoves the stock-location-form-workspace adapter. It only opened the\ncreate location modal, which the locations table already opens directly,\nand nothing launches it.\n\nAdds a mockWorkspace2Props test helper to __mocks__ so tests can render\nworkspaces with the full v2 prop set.\n\n* (fix) Revalidate stock management data through the framework's SWR cache\n\nhandleMutate called the global `mutate` exported by swr. That function is\nbound to SWR's default cache. The framework's openmrsComponentDecorator\nwraps every component in an SWRConfig whose provider is a shared,\nmodule-level cache, and the useSWR hooks in this app read from that cache.\nhandleMutate therefore matched no keys, so the table refresh actions and\nthe revalidation after saves and deletes never refetched anything.\n\nReplace handleMutate with a useHandleMutate hook. The hook takes `mutate`\nfrom useSWRConfig(), which is bound to the cache of the nearest SWRConfig,\nand returns a function that revalidates every string key starting with the\ngiven URL. The 16 components that called handleMutate now call the hook\nand use the returned function. The call sites and URL prefixes are\nunchanged. The returned function is added to the useCallback dependency\narrays that reference it.\n\nAdd a test for useHandleMutate that renders useSWR under an SWRConfig with\nits own cache provider and checks that only the matching key is refetched.\nUpdate the stock items table and stock source delete tests to mock the\nhook. The delete test now triggers the component's own onConfirmation\nhandler instead of calling the mock directly.\n\n* Drop the redundant revalidate option from useHandleMutate\n\nSWR's mutate revalidates matched keys unless revalidate is explicitly false, so passing { revalidate: true } has no effect. The explicit undefined data argument stays, so the call still takes the same path through SWR's mutate.\n\n* Revalidate stock rules after saving a rule\n\nThe stock rule form is now a child workspace, so the stock item\nworkspace stays mounted underneath it. Closing the rule form after a\nsave returned to the Rules tab with the old list, because nothing\nrevalidated the stock rule query.\n\nThe save handler now revalidates every stockmanagement/stockrule key\nbefore closing. It uses the mutate from useSWRConfig rather than the\nhandleMutate helper. handleMutate calls the global mutate exported by\nswr, which is bound to SWR's default cache, while the framework gives\ndecorated components their own shared cache. So handleMutate doesn't\nreach the rule list's query.\n\n* Use useHandleMutate to revalidate stock rules after saving\n\nReplace the inline useSWRConfig().mutate call and its URL-prefix key filter with the useHandleMutate hook from src/utils.ts, which does the same revalidation through the framework's SWR cache. This matches how the rest of the app revalidates after saves and deletes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3c071999ea6f2b75706d5ba602caeba07ec55a02","date":"2026-07-06T18:26:40+03:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#566) (#567)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Josephkagimu1","authorEmail":"88326256+Josephkagimu1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c67e47060f34697bd5e9aa63389a35fc5df2eed8","date":"2026-05-05T09:15:40+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality (#541)","refs":"","body":"* O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality\n\n* Response to Comments","authorName":"Lubwama Samuel","authorEmail":"lubwamasamuel3@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f6fc80647842ad34e8364caae0e84d9c880f7505","date":"2026-02-08T10:45:09+03:00","message":"fix stock location underfetching (#452)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"150463eed63dcbb7606e137445d6e53a684741fe","date":"2025-12-19T11:33:22+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve Carbon component type safety and code quality (#409)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Improve Carbon component type safety and code quality\n\nCarbon component type safety improvements:\n- Extend ControlledComboBox with ComboBoxProps<ItemType> generics for type-safe items\n- Use Omit to prevent prop conflicts (onChange, id, ref, value) in controlled components\n- Fix ControlledRadioButtonGroup to use valueSelected prop instead of value\n- Remove invalid props (name, control, controllerName) spread to Carbon components\n- Add CustomTableHeader and CustomTableRow interfaces for type-safe DataTables\n- Delete unused ControlledDropdown component and clean up module declarations\n\nTranslation & i18n:\n- Replace hardcoded strings with translation keys in table download menu\n- Add proper i18n for pagination controls (nextPage, previousPage)\n- Standardize download menu labels to consistent title case\n- Improve label consistency (Batch number, Quantity labels)\n\nBug fixes & typos:\n- Fix \"aprove\" → \"approve\" in TASK_STOCKMANAGEMENT_STOCKOPERATIONS_APPROVE\n- Fix \"ADMNISTRATOR\" → \"ADMINISTRATOR\" in INVENTORY_ADMINISTRATOR_ROLE_UUID\n- Fix \"Item already exits\" → \"Item already exists\"\n- Fix \"deletePackagingUnitMesaage\" → \"deletePackagingUnitMessage\"\n\nCode quality:\n- Improve DataTable render pattern (render prop → children)\n- Clean up unused imports and variables (inputValue in drug-selector)\n- Reorder imports for consistency\n- Remove unnecessary @carbon/react module declaration\n- Better prop destructuring to avoid shadowing in controlled components\n\n* Fixup\n\n* Review feedback","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"cc09d606aa2e7d8bfcacc9cb54bda34cea6336a4","date":"2025-05-19T08:34:49+03:00","message":"(fix) Fix translations and UI consistency (#293)","refs":"","body":"This PR makes the following changes:\n\n- Replace TabPanel components with semantic h2 headers across all table components\n- Add standardized tableHeader styling with consistent margins and typography\n- Update translation keys to be more specific and descriptive\n- Standardize capitalization in translations\n- Remove redundant translation key\n\nThis change improves UI consistency, accessibility, and maintainability across the stock management module.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"33428cb1c4c192f1a1701855de8f7c0006982fc8","date":"2025-05-18T12:49:43+03:00","message":"(refactor) Improve component organization and naming consistency (#291)","refs":"","body":"This PR makes the following changes:\n\n- Flatten component directory structure by moving files up one level\n- Remove empty/unused files (.resource.tsx, .scss, .test.tsx)\n- Change .resource.tsx to .resource.ts where no JSX is used\n- Fix typo: PrivilagedView → PrivilegedView\n- Make modal names more specific (e.g., DeleteConfirmation → DeleteStockSourceModal)\n- Update import paths to match new file structure\n\nThis refactoring improves code organization and maintainability while preserving existing functionality.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b20f85d0eb11170c0577c24f13bd9b1e7e70e264","date":"2025-05-16T14:57:33+03:00","message":"(feat) Additional visual tweaks (#285)","refs":"","body":"This PR makes a few visual adjustments to the User role scopes table UI. These include:\n\n- Replacing the Carbon `Button` component used in the delete and edit actions menu with the `IconButton` component. This allows us to take advantage of the IconButton's spacing, alignment, and tooltip features.\n- Adding consistent sizing and spacing for arrow icons in the Locations column.\n- Updating translation keys for better consistency.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jabar Jeremy <24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f0dc782b6761b9fa3472c9680275ca3048a87450","date":"2025-05-15T15:27:41+03:00","message":"Restore: (fix) Various test and styling fixes (#282) (#283)","refs":"","body":"* Revert \"Revert \"(fix) Various test and styling fixes (#282)\"\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3e99c7e84649795b40bb4ff14c2a6d3d5b3a2862.\n\n* Fixup\n\n* Additional fixes","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3e99c7e84649795b40bb4ff14c2a6d3d5b3a2862","date":"2025-05-15T11:57:03+03:00","message":"Revert \"(fix) Various test and styling fixes (#282)\"","refs":"","body":"This reverts commit 340f6f0fc0dd4cc33183c58894e9f82e8527d4de.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"340f6f0fc0dd4cc33183c58894e9f82e8527d4de","date":"2025-05-15T08:26:37+03:00","message":"(fix) Various test and styling fixes (#282)","refs":"","body":"This commit applies several enhancements to the Stock Management test suite, including:\n\n- Refactoring manual mocks in tests to match our mocking patterns best practices https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/frontend-modules/unit-and-integration-testing#mocking-patterns\n- Removing unnecessary mocks in favor of using the actual implementation for things like the useTranslation hook\n- Properly annotating mocks with type annotations\n- Adding path aliases for the top-level `mocks` and `tools` directories to make imports cleaner and more readable\n- Fixing Carbon component prop errors so we end up with a test console clear of errors and warnings\n\nOther changes in the diff include:\n\n- Setting the max-width of the TableToolbarAction to `none` to constrain the width of the refresh button\n- Updating the react-i18next manual mock to align with what we have across other O3 repos for consistency\n- Reorganizing imports in components to match best practices","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3b4d0080b66dee8c40e864dcdfe75705eaf29113","date":"2025-05-14T18:46:05+03:00","message":"(feat) Stock operations table UI enhancements (#280)","refs":"","body":"Applies several UI enhancements to the stock operations table, including:\n- Adding labels to the range datepicker\n- Improving the toolbar layout and styling\n- Cleaning up duplicate styles\n\nOther broader changes include:\n\n- Reorganize imports to match conventions\n- Improving code formatting\n- Removing the `~` prefix from @openmrs/esm-styleguide imports an","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0992ce9aff66ddb5a8d3e347d97dd6e810dbc827","date":"2025-05-13T21:59:54+03:00","message":"Fixup (#277)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Earl Munyua","authorEmail":"142984533+Munyua123@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"0380b1548481258450bfb5b3803e10738e13dba0","date":"2025-05-12T20:24:35+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-4685: Use workspaces instead of overlays (#268)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n","authorName":"Jabar Jeremy","authorEmail":"24471994+jabahum@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a01a24ceedd14744164d7dbe952466ea254308a1","date":"2025-05-09T09:31:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Enforce consistent type imports (#272)","refs":"","body":"This commit enforces consistent type imports across the project using the eslint import plugin and adds the `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports` rule with the `inline-type-imports` fixStyle. It converts hundreds of import statements across the codebase to follow the explicit `import { type X }` pattern, and simplifies the `lint` script by removing the `cross-env` dependency.\n\nThis change improves code clarity by distinguishing between value and type imports and potentially improves build performance by enabling better tree-shaking of type-only imports.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6d003fb2cacae0e4ea9f3f9a1a8e5dd3dd648697","date":"2025-05-01T19:08:34+03:00","message":"(chore) Bump @carbon/react to v1.76.0 (#265)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9bc102b619114739f5d7fb4264079dbe8e59b4cc","date":"2025-02-24T18:12:22+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-4475: Rename the Operations empty state (#259)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Samuel Muli","authorEmail":"136758902+Samstar10@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2088daede22c8ace6ca49c1ad7c9c3ce845405e7","date":"2024-09-27T00:16:40+03:00","message":"(refactor) Destructure error and isLoading variables from SWR hooks (#224)","refs":"","body":"* (refactor) Destructure error and isLoading variables from SWR hooks\r\n\r\nThis PR refactors some SWR-based hooks to correctly destructure the `error` and `isLoading` variables directly from the hooks.\r\nThese hooks were previously setting an `isError` variable, which was incorrect as the `error` property returned by SWR is an Error object, not a boolean.\r\nIt also fixes some instances where the `isLoading` variable was not being used.\r\n\r\nIt also restores husky, which should fix the pre-commit and pre-push hooks.\r\n\r\n* Fixup","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"dd1a73ea1a9eb46ff34b36a723feb3d27c90af11","date":"2024-09-25T23:02:17+03:00","message":"(chore) Fix react-hooks/exhaustive-deps warnings (#219)","refs":"","body":"This PR fixes various react-hooks/exhaustive-deps warnings in this project, ensuring that all hooks are properly memoized and dependencies are correctly specified.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4f398ca2ffe303d0dc14c3518f62545bc36f92d7","date":"2024-09-25T19:20:49+03:00","message":"(chore) Set up Prettier and separate formatting and linting concerns (#216)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bbb56d3ae9a50019764065b6ab85c432618dead0","date":"2024-08-29T11:09:12+03:00","message":"Update Carbon styling imports and tokens in stock management (#207)","refs":"","body":"* Update Carbon styling imports and tokens in stock management\r\n\r\n* PR comments","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"61805ca674dfa154be6ef0082e6d2242d5bd5f5f","date":"2024-08-14T15:43:48+03:00","message":"(fix): Fix undefined thrown when selecting an operation (#193)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Makombe Kennedy","authorEmail":"kennedy